# Pepto – Production Monitoring (KT2)

## Overview
This session focused on production monitoring activities for the Pepto platform, covering application health, data pipelines, cron jobs, data flow validation, alerts, and cache monitoring.

## Business Context
Pepto receives data from multiple client applications and processes it through various pipelines before serving it to downstream consumers. Continuous monitoring is required to ensure reliability and data accuracy.

## Monitoring Scope and Responsibilities
- Monitor application auto-scaling and pod utilization.
- Validate cron job executions and log generation.
- Monitor archive, delta, remediation, and validation pipelines.
- Ensure continuous data flow from all clients.
- Monitor Redis cache health and capacity.
- Investigate alerts and coordinate with upstream teams.

## Application and Pod Monitoring
Applications have defined minimum and maximum pod limits. Normal pod ranges are observed, and sudden spikes require investigation of request volume, latency, and pod failures.

## Cron Job Monitoring
Cron jobs run for PDS and Facade applications, mainly handling Geo data updates into Redis. Monitoring involves checking job success status and validating expected daily log counts in OpenSearch.

## Data Pipeline Monitoring
Pipelines run either daily or every two hours depending on data volume. Monitoring focuses on execution success, runtime behavior, and bad record counts. Large anomalies trigger deeper analysis.

## Missing Hours and Data Validation
Dedicated pipelines detect missing hourly data. Failures generate alerts, and investigations include checking S3 paths, application health, and upstream sources.

## Alerts and Firehose Monitoring
CloudWatch alarms monitor data flow thresholds. Short-lived alerts may be ignored, while prolonged drops lead to detailed root cause analysis.

## Redis Cache Monitoring
Redis cache utilization is closely monitored, especially memory usage. Utilization beyond critical thresholds requires proactive action to avoid outages.

## Outcome
The session provided a hands-on understanding of Pepto production monitoring processes and prepared team members for ongoing production support duties.
